import json
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];c=json.loads(Path('/mnt/c/Users/RkLop/.codex/skills/uliya-skill-kit/data/capability-catalog.json').read_text())
p=root/'research/12-self-healing-archive/action-capability-audit.md'
intro='''# Official action capability audit\n\nCatalog `2.0.0`, generated 2026-09-01, installed Uliya Skill Creation Tool. Source: `/mnt/c/Users/RkLop/.codex/skills/uliya-skill-kit/data/capability-catalog.json`, `references/expert-orchestration.md`, `cli-usage-rules.md`, `safety-and-approval.md`, `completion-and-errors.md`; [official starter kit](https://ai.ugreen.com/pages/hackathon-starter-kit); [rules](https://ugreenhackathon.devpost.com/rules). Accessed 2026-10-26. The catalog is a generation-time contract, not proof that a device implements these operations. Every row shows **all documented parameters**, where `*` denotes required. Return descriptions are copied from the catalog and may be incomplete or corrupted; blanks are not fields we may invent. Names are clues to purpose, not detailed semantics. Read source JSON for parameter types/enums.\n\nEvery child can return `completed`, `failed`, `cancelled`, `waiting_user`, or `waiting_approval`; dependent work requires completed and sufficient business data. The generic internal CLI envelope is `{ok,data}` or `{ok,error}`; it is **not** guaranteed to be the parent's expert result. Catalog says permissions, prerequisites, error codes and stability are unknown. Gateway/workflow/conditional approval is enforced by the child/platform; the user must explicitly approve our proposed modification. Read actions are marked no approval in catalog, not blanket authorization to access arbitrary data. Retry/idempotency and undo are not documented for any action; never assume either, especially for writes. Read-back verification is possible where separate listing/stat/hash/content/album query supports it, but interpretation and completeness remain unverified; absence or an error is not proven nonexistence. `restore` example concerns a recycle path, not general versioned rollback.\n\n**Feasibility answer:** A read → propose → approve → one copy → read-back workflow is compositionally documented, but its successful execution, approval and safe no-overwrite semantics are not yet verified on actual UGREEN hardware. The prototype must stop if the child cannot ensure no overwrite; precheck alone is vulnerable to races. `cpmv` supports `type=copy|move` and `overwrite` (boolean), but the catalog does not document collision/atomicity, destination interpretation or default overwrite behavior. `ls`, `stat`, `sha256sum` support independent checks, but not a guarantee of complete dependencies. `file-workflow:batch-move` is workflow-approved and reports status/total/succeeded/failed/renamedFiles/hasMore; semantics and propagation to the parent remain unknown. `ug-knowledge:save-text` documents verified/outputFile/contentBytes as CLI return summary but parent expert propagation is unknown. The catalog has `mkdir`, `del`, `rename`, `echo`, `touch`, `restore`, and tagging; none imply general undo or safe automatic deduplication. `scan-dedupe` is a read operation; deletion is separately approved. Photo albums are catalog state changes; exact persistence, contents and results remain unverified.\n\n## All registered families and actions\n\n| Family → owner | Action / catalog description | Required and optional parameters | Effect / approval | Return summary / verification |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n'''
lines=[]
for cl in c['clis']:
 for a in cl['actions']:
  desc=a.get('description','').replace('|','/').replace('\n',' ')
  params=', '.join('`'+x['name']+('*' if x.get('required') else '')+'`' for x in a.get('parameters',[])) or 'none'
  ret=str(a.get('returnSummary','not specified')).replace('|','/').replace('\n',' ') or 'not specified'
  lines.append(f"| `{cl['name']}` → `{cl['agent']}` | `{a['name']}` / {desc} | {params} | {a.get('effect','unknown')} / {a.get('approval','unknown')} | {ret} |")
p.write_text(intro+'\n'.join(lines)+'''\n\n## Interpretation and verification\n\n- Files: `ls`, `find`, `stat`, `cat`, `sha256sum`, `md5sum`, `getfattr` are catalog read actions; hash equality is byte evidence, not semantic equivalence or dependency analysis. `category` can list categories. `cpmv` supports copy/move; `rename`, `del`, `mkdir`, `echo`, `touch`, `chtimes`, `restore`, `share-mkdir` are state-changing. Inspect with `ls`/`stat`/hash/cat where permitted, but there is no documented atomic transaction or undo.\n- File management: `scan-dedupe` is a scan, not removal. Tag actions mutate metadata; tag-add-file/tag-delete-file have conditional approval, whose exact conditions are undocumented. Read tags with the corresponding get/list actions, if returned.\n- Document: `qa`, `extract`, `metadata`, `page-count`, `reconcile` inspect; `writing` and `translate` are mixed/gateway, with creation/edit details unverified; neither implies in-place repair of arbitrary documents.\n- Knowledge: collect-evidence, official answer and audio transcription are reads; save-text is workflow-approved. No arbitrary persistent graph, provenance completeness or in-place rewrite guarantee is established.\n- Photo: read/search/meta/vision and album inspection are documented; `create-album*` and `timeline` are catalog state-change/workflow. `albums`/`album-detail` may support inspection, not guaranteed post-write verification or return schemas.\n- Media: video/music search are mixed even if some queries may only inspect; play/control changes playback state. Video subtitle download has gateway approval; verify as available via read-back, do not invent paths or IDs. Surveillance actions are sensitive read capabilities; none are needed for the MVP.\n\n**Approval nuance:** No catalog approval value guarantees owner consent for broad search. Actual user-authorized scope and platform enforcement are separate. User refusal, pending authorization, cancellation or incomplete return must stop. Real post-write checks, source paths/excerpts, pagination/coverage, resumability, exact platform UI, permission failures and target filesystem collisions require device testing.\n''')
print(len(lines),'actions documented')
